cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Tech Bros to Cowboys: How Much Better Off Are Californians Who Move to Texas?"
abstract: >-
  Compares recent California-to-Texas movers against Californians who stayed,
  using ACS microdata (2021-2023) and BEA regional price parities. Holding
  demographics, education, and household composition fixed, movers have
  income relative to a locally-priced poverty threshold 10.1% higher
  (95% CI 3.7% to 16.9%). Against the unadjusted federal threshold there is
  no detectable difference. Descriptive, not causal.
